<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Connections among Different Diffusion Models.</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The diffusion model we define in this paper can be reformulated to align with other common diffusion frameworks, such as DDPM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Smld</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song &amp; Ermon, 2019</a>)</cite>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ve-sde</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>)</cite> and <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Vp-sde</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, as well as with approaches like x-prediction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, v-prediction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Salimans &amp; Ho, 2022</a>)</cite>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-prediction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.
This demonstrates that our formulation is compatible with diverse diffusion paradigms while facilitating unified theoretical analysis.
To better demonstrate this transformation, we present the following pseudocodes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DDPM.</span>
DDPM define a sequence <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\sqrt{\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\sqrt{\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which can be seen as a special case of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Background ‣ Learning Robust Diffusion Models from Imprecise Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) where we can set <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=\sqrt{\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=\sqrt{\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=\sqrt{1-\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=\sqrt{1-\prod_{i=0}^{t}(1-\beta_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Smld<span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Smld</span> defines a noise schedule <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sigma(t)\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sigma(t)\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(1)&lt;\sigma(2)&lt;\cdots&lt;\sigma(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(1)&lt;\sigma(2)&lt;\cdots&lt;\sigma(T)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this setup, Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Background ‣ Learning Robust Diffusion Models from Imprecise Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) reduces to <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=\sigma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=\sigma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Vp-sde<span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Vp-sde</span> is the continuous case of DDPM, which define a stochastic differential equation (SDE) as</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dX_{t}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)X_{t}dt+\sqrt{\beta(t)}dW_{t},\quad t\in[0,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}=-\frac{1}{2}\beta(t)X_{t}dt+\sqrt{\beta(t)}dW_{t},\quad t\in[0,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)=\beta_{t\cdot T}\cdot T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)=\beta_{t\cdot T}\cdot T</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this setup, <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=\sqrt{\exp\left(-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)ds\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=\sqrt{\exp\left(-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)ds\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{t}={1-\exp\left(-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)ds\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}={1-\exp\left(-\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)ds\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Ve-sde<span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span> <span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ve-sde</span> is the continuous case of <span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Smld</span>, whose forward process of <span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ve-sde</span> is defined as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dX_{t}=\sqrt{\frac{d\sigma(t)^{2}}{dt}}\,dW_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}=\sqrt{\frac{d\sigma(t)^{2}}{dt}}\,dW_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">In this setup, <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(t)-\sigma^{2}(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(t)-\sigma^{2}(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">While the models above each define their own specific frameworks for the diffusion process, EDM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>)</cite> proposes a unified structure and optimizes the parameters choice within the diffusion process, making it both robust and adaptable.
Therefore, for our implementation, we adopt EDM as the foundational diffusion model.
In EDM, the scaling and noise schedules are a special case of <span id="A2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ve-sde</span>, where the variance of the noise is given by <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)=t</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, we use <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}/\alpha_{t},\sigma_{t}/\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}/\alpha_{t},\sigma_{t}/\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the predicted score, as shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ B.1 Connections among Different Diffusion Models. ‣ Appendix B Proof ‣ Learning Robust Diffusion Models from Imprecise Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Our models to EDM</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            A score network <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, a noisy input <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, noise level <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, linear schedule <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Calculate the denoised image <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}=(\mathbf{x}_{t}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}/\alpha_{t},{\sigma_{t}}/{\alpha_{t}}\right))/\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}=(\mathbf{x}_{t}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{s}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}/\alpha_{t},{\sigma_{t}}/{\alpha_{t}}\right))/\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> performing <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-prediction <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            Calculate the noise component <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}=\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0}}{\sigma_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}=\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0}}{\sigma_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> performing <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>-prediction <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            Calculate the noise component <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}=\alpha_{t}\bm{\epsilon}-\sigma_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}=\alpha_{t}\bm{\epsilon}-\sigma_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> performing <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}</annotation></semantics></math>-prediction <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Derivation of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2 Background ‣ Learning Robust Diffusion Models from Imprecise Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximizing the variational lower bound, or equivalently evidence lower bound (ELBO), to optimize the diffusion model is a common approach. To avoid redundant proofs, we directly use the conclusion from Eq. (58) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo (2022)</a></cite> as below:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})\!\geq\!\mathbb{E}_{q}[-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\mathbf{x}_{T}|\mathbf{x}_{0})\|p(\mathbf{x}_{T}))\!+\!\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{0}|\mathbf{x}_{1})\!-\!\!\sum_{t&gt;1}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})\|p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})\!\geq\!\mathbb{E}_{q}[-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\mathbf{x}_{T}|\mathbf{x}_{0})\|p(\mathbf{x}_{T}))\!+\!\log p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{0}|\mathbf{x}_{1})\!-\!\!\sum_{t&gt;1}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})\|p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Although each KL divergence term <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})\|p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})\|p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> is difficult to minimize for arbitrary posteriors, we can leverage the Gaussian transition assumption to make optimization tractable. By Bayes rule, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})=\frac{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})=\frac{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As we already know that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> from Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Background ‣ Learning Robust Diffusion Models from Imprecise Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> can be derived from its equivalent form <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}(\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t-1}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}^{*}}{\alpha_{t-1}})+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}(\frac{\mathbf{x}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t-1}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}^{*}}{\alpha_{t-1}})+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1}+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\sigma_{t-1}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1}+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\sigma_{t-1}\bm{\epsilon}_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1}+\sqrt{\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2}}\bm{\epsilon}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1}+\sqrt{\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2}}\bm{\epsilon}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t};\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2}\mathbf{I})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t};\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2}\mathbf{I}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now, knowing the forms of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can proceed to calculate the form of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by substituting into the Bayes rule expansion:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})=\frac{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{0})=\frac{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{0})q(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}{q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t};\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\sqrt{\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2}}\mathbf{I})\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1};\alpha_{t-1}\mathbf{x}_{0},\sigma_{t-1}\mathbf{I})}{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t};\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0},\sigma_{t}\mathbf{I})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t};\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1},\sqrt{\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2}}\mathbf{I})\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1};\alpha_{t-1}\mathbf{x}_{0},\sigma_{t-1}\mathbf{I})}{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x}_{t};\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0},\sigma_{t}\mathbf{I})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∝</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left\{-\left[\frac{(\mathbf{x}_{t}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1})^{2}}{2(\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2})}+\frac{(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}-\alpha_{t-1}\mathbf{x}_{0})^{2}}{2\sigma_{t-1}^{2}}-\frac{(\mathbf{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0})^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right]\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left\{-\left[\frac{(\mathbf{x}_{t}-\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}\mathbf{x}_{t-1})^{2}}{2(\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t-1}^{2}}\sigma_{t-1}^{2})}+\frac{(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}-\alpha_{t-1}\mathbf{x}_{0})^{2}}{2\sigma_{t-1}^{2}}-\frac{(\mathbf{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}_{0})^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right]\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
